 ## Background
-Originating from the need to render dynamic scenes in real-time, these methods build on [3D Gaussian Splatting](9128-3d-gaussian-splatting-implementation-details.md) [G]. [Deformable 3D Gaussians](16260-deformable-3d-gaussians.md) addresses limitations of implicit methods (slow convergence, overfitting) by using explicit Gaussians with a deformation field. [SpacetimeGaussians Training Pipeline](15898-spacetimegaussians-training-pipeline.md) and [Spacetime Gaussian Feature Splatting](16313-spacetime-gaussian-feature-splatting.md) further explore parametric and feature-based temporal modeling. [Rendering-aware QP Offset Modelling](21036-rendering-aware-qp-offset-modelling.md) extends the family to address rate-distortion optimization for compressed streaming.
+The extension of 3D Gaussian Splatting to dynamic scenes emerged to address the limitations of implicit neural representations (like NeRF) in real-time rendering and the inability of static 3DGS to handle motion. Deformable 3D Gaussians [S1] and Spacetime Gaussian Feature Splatting  represent key developments in decoupling geometry deformation from appearance. These methods are used in applications requiring high-fidelity dynamic scene reconstruction, such as virtual production, autonomous driving simulation, and dynamic novel view synthesis [S1].
 
